From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] winex11, win32u: the keyboard tables follow the activated layout, not the X keyboard map (6000)

MapVirtualKeyEx, VkKeyScanEx, ToUnicodeEx, GetKeyNameText and the virtual keys
of typed keys were answered from the X keyboard map whatever layout (HKL) a
program activated or named, so a program that activated French while X had a
US map got US answers (dinput device8: 47 per-layout failures, KBD-HKL).

When an HKL asks for a layout the X map is not (not the session's own layout,
not the X map's XKB layout), winex11 now builds that layout's tables from its
XKB description (xkbcommon, rules evdev, the same data the X server compiles)
and hands them to win32u (KbdLayerDescriptor), which answers from them. Virtual
keys follow the Windows layouts: a key gets the letter it types, other keys
keep the US virtual key, except the OEM keys kbdfr and kbdgr assign their own
way. AltGr is Ctrl+Alt (KLLF_ALTGR). Keys typed while such a layout is active
get its virtual key for their scan code, so WM_CHAR follows the layout too.
win32u: dead keys (WCH_DEAD entries followed by their 0xff character entry):
MapVirtualKey VK_TO_CHAR marks them with the top bit (MapVirtualKeyExA keeps
the mark), ToUnicodeEx returns -1 with the character; VkKeyScanEx takes the key
needing the fewest modifiers and ignores the Caps Lock (SGCAPS) entries; the
VK_TO_CHAR table holds whole characters (it truncated them to a byte).
Not done: dead-key composition with the next key (ToUnicodeEx returns the
spacing character only), layout ids (0xfXXX HKLs) keep the X map.
